/// Transport — the socket operations Catalina needs from a transport, as in
/// Thousand Island's `ThousandIsland.Transport` behaviour.
///
/// A transport is a class with class-side methods only (`TCPTransport`,
/// `SSLTransport`), so every requirement here is a `class` method.
/// Conformance is structural: a class conforms when it answers all of them.
///
/// Expected failures answer `Result error:` holding the **bare Erlang
/// reason**, as Thousand Island's `{:error, reason}`: usually a Symbol
/// (`#closed`, `#timeout`, `#econnreset`, `#eaddrinuse`), possibly a Tuple
/// (some SSL alerts), so the error side is typed `Object`. An FFI call's
/// `{error, R}` arrives as an Exception (ADR 0076), so an implementation
/// normalises it once, at this boundary, with `mapError: [:e | e reason]`
/// (BT-3954). A stub answers its reason directly (`Result error:
/// #not_secure`). Callers compare the error itself:
/// `(TCPTransport recv: s length: 0 timeout: 100) error =:= #timeout`.
///
/// **Seal the class and every class method** (`sealed Object subclass:`,
/// `class sealed`). A class method of an open or stateful class runs in the
/// class's own process, not the caller's (ADR 0129), and socket calls must
/// run in the caller: `controllingProcess:pid:` and `sendfile:...` only work
/// from the socket's owner, and a blocking `accept:` or `recv:...` in the
/// class process would serialise every acceptor and handler behind one
/// process.
///
/// A transport may also answer `handshake:timeout:`. `Socket handshake`
/// prefers it when present and otherwise falls back to `handshake:`, as
/// Thousand Island does with its optional `handshake/2` callback.
///
/// ## Examples
/// ```beamtalk
/// TCPTransport conformsTo: #Transport   // => true
/// ```
Protocol define: Transport
  /// Open a listen socket on `port` (0 for an ephemeral port).
  class listen: port :: Integer options: options :: List(Symbol | Tuple) -> Result(Port | Tuple, Object)

  /// Wait for a connection on a listen socket.
  class accept: listenSocket :: Object -> Result(Port | Tuple, Object)

  /// Complete the transport's handshake on a new connection (TLS); a clear
  /// transport answers the socket unchanged.
  class handshake: socket :: Object -> Result(Port | Tuple, Object)

  /// Upgrade an established connection (STARTTLS-style), or answer
  /// `Result error: #unsupported_upgrade`.
  class upgrade: socket :: Object options: options :: Object -> Result(Port | Tuple, Object)

  /// Hand the socket to `pid`. Only its current owner may call this.
  class controllingProcess: socket :: Object pid: pid :: Pid -> Result(Nil, Object)

  /// Read up to `length` bytes (0: whatever is available), waiting at most
  /// `timeout` ms (or `#infinity`).
  class recv: socket :: Object length: length :: Integer timeout: timeout :: Object -> Result(Binary, Object)

  /// Send a String or iodata.
  class send: socket :: Object data: data :: Object -> Result(Nil, Object)

  /// Send `length` bytes of a file from `offset` (0 for the rest of it).
  class sendfile: socket :: Object filename: filename :: String offset: offset :: Integer length: length :: Integer -> Result(Integer, Object)

  /// Read socket options.
  class getopts: socket :: Object options: options :: List(Symbol | Tuple) -> Result(List(Symbol | Tuple), Object)

  /// Set socket options.
  class setopts: socket :: Object options: options :: List(Symbol | Tuple) -> Result(Nil, Object)

  /// Shut the connection down in one direction: `#read`, `#write` or `#read_write`.
  class shutdown: socket :: Object how: way :: Symbol -> Result(Nil, Object)

  /// Close a connection or listen socket.
  class close: socket :: Object -> Result(Nil, Object)

  /// The local `{ip, port}` of a connection or listen socket.
  class sockname: socket :: Object -> Result(SocketAddress, Object)

  /// The remote `{ip, port}` of a connection.
  class peername: socket :: Object -> Result(SocketAddress, Object)

  /// The peer's DER certificate, or `Result error: #not_secure`.
  class peercert: socket :: Object -> Result(Binary, Object)

  /// Whether this transport is encrypted.
  class isSecure -> Boolean

  /// The socket's `inet:getstat/1` counters.
  class getstat: socket :: Object -> Result(List(Tuple(Symbol, Integer)), Object)

  /// The ALPN protocol, or `Result error: #protocol_not_negotiated`.
  class negotiatedProtocol: socket :: Object -> Result(String, Object)

  /// The TLS connection information, or `Result error: #not_secure`.
  class connectionInformation: socket :: Object -> Result(List(Tuple), Object)
